AB  - This article describes a developmental model of intervention for multiple DUI offenders, the Paradigm Developmental Model of Treatment (PDMT). Drawing on a variety of intervention models, the PDMT provides a framework for counselors to help move clients through a series of four 'paradigm shifts' which utilize themes extrapolated from the 12 steps of Alcoholics Anonymous. A paradigm shift includes changes in the way one views one's self and the world and responds to it. Continued assessment of motivation to change within each paradigm is critical. Examples are given of how these shifts are encouraged and a case example is provided.
