AB  - Since the introduction of the Mental Treatment Act 1930 there has been an emphasis on the voluntary treatment of mental disorder. However, recently a succession of proposals have aimed at extending compulsory treatment to patients living in the community. These ideas have gained considerable support from the medical establishment but they are seriously flawed and if implemented could be unworkable. In this paper the various proposals are examined, the arguments for and against them are discussed and the relevant literature is reviewed. Reprinted by permission of Taylor and Francis Ltd.
