AB  - Administered Diagnostic Personality Questionnaire 74/M (DPQ) 3 times to 27 male alcoholics (mean age 36.7 yrs old) during their 1st mo of hospitalization for alcoholism treatment. The test consists of 2 control scales (G and Y) and 8 clinical scales measuring hypochondriasis, depression, conversion, hysteria, psychopathy, social hypersensitivity, psychasthenia, schizophrenia, and manic symptoms. Ss underwent detoxification treatment the 1st 10–24 days and then individual and group psychotherapy. The DPQ was administered the day after admission, 2 wks later, and again 2 wks later. Changes in Ss' personality profiles were evident during the 1st 14 days of treatment. During detoxification, increased anxiety, hypochondria, and lack of desire for social interaction were observed. The levels of hypochondria and anxiety diminished after treatment. The personality profiles were characterized by increased psychopathy compared with healthy individuals. (English & Russian abstracts) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2019 APA, all rights reserved)
