AB  - In response to a change in reimbursement incentives, hospitals may change the intensity of services provided to a given set of patients, change the type (or severity) of patients they see, or change their market share. Each of these 3 responses, defined as moral hazard effect, a selection effect, and a practice-style effect, can influence average resource use in a population. A methodology for disentangling these effects is developed and implemented, using a panel data set of Medicaid psychiatric discharges in New Hampshire.
