AB  - The article presents the author's reply to the comment about his article on the comparative effectiveness of community clinic and psychiatric hospital treatment. He reiterates his position that there is no consistent evidence that community treatment of mentally ill patients is more effective than hospital treatment. He explains that the use of residual scores in measuring treatment outcome of groups that have no equivalence is robust and that violating other theoretical assumptions made little difference in the correlation obtained.
