AB  - Symptoms of acute stress, posttraumatic stress syndrome, & stages of recovery in Canadian crime victims are discussed based on personal experience as a social worker. Reactions of victims during & shortly after victimization are cited. Four principal stages are identified in the recovery process: shock, retrospective, regain of control, & recovery. It is suggested that recovery is directly related to the sympathy & support the victim receives after the crime. Effective interventions are described: group or individual discussion of the traumatizing event, long- or short-term individual consultation, & support groups. 15 References. Adapted from the source document.
