AB  - Data obtained via participant observation & interviews are used to examine identity transformations among 30 members of 2 weight loss therapy groups. It is shown that the loss of weight is but one of a number of issues that the obese dieter deals with as he or she assumes the identity of a thin person. Once dieters have lost weight & achieved their ideal of thinness, they are often disappointed at the negative impact their new identity has on acquaintances & loved ones, which in turn effects a return to "normalcy" via a return to obesity. It is concluded that social factors in the dieter's world have a significant impact on the degree of weight loss achieved & on the likelihood of maintaining an idealized weight. 16 References. Adapted from the source document.
