AB  - Group therapy by telephone was provided to 42 blind veterans (aged 56–78 yrs) to provide a format for problem solving and treatment for affective disorder related to isolation. Pre- and posttreatment measures included the Personal Assessment of Role Skills, Wakefield Self-Assessment Depression Inventory, and UCLA Loneliness Scale. Significant decreases in loneliness and an increase in activity level were attributed to therapeutic intervention by telephone. (16 ref) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
