AB  - Tested the hypothesis that the relation between adjustment prior to treatment and client outcome is curvilinear. 77 outpatients at a university-affiliated hospital completed a depression inventory, the UCLA Loneliness Scale, the Life Satisfaction Index, and a goal attainment scale. Findings show that there was no curvilinear relationship between prior adjustment and outcome; however, a linear relationship between expectation and self-assessed outcome was observed. (11 ref) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
