AB  - Veterans may have experienced challenging combat situations which may result in being diagnosed with mental illnesses such as post-traumatic stress disorder, depression and substance abuse disorder. Agencies such as U.S. VETS-Long Beach provide many services to support such veterans as they transition into civilian life. The academic literature provides evidence that music therapy is a beneficial intervention for veterans diagnosed with mental illness. However, many agencies, including U.S. VETS-Long Beach, lack funding for music therapy groups. The purpose of this project is to create a grant proposal that may be submitted on behalf of U.S. VETS-Long Beach to obtain funding for group music therapy services for veterans diagnosed with mental illness. The actual submission and/or funding of this grant was not a requirement for the successful completion of the project. Copies of dissertations may be obtained by addressing your request to ProQuest, 789 E. Eisenhower Parkway, P.O. Box 1346, Ann Arbor, MI 48106-1346. Telephone 1-800-521-3042; e-mail: disspub@umi.com
