AB  - The article focuses on the study of a university-based comprehensive community mental health center operating as a multi-disciplinary training facility, which involved psychologists and psychiatrists. The training program focused on the history and conditions of cooperative works between university-based comprehensive community mental health centers and university departments for multi-disciplinary training program developments. It credits a study of the Orange-Person-Chatham Mental Health Center. The institution developed several effective strategies, like joint seminars and trainee participation which exposed students to mental health practices.
