AB  - Alcohol is a "somewhat neglected drug". Alcohol consumption in Europe is high (double, compared to the rest of the world) and there is a huge gap between problematic alcohol use and alcohol treatment. European Committee through CNAPA (Committee on National Alcohol Planning and Action) and RARHA (Joint Action on Reducing Alcohol Related Harm) is planning and performing interventions especially for vulnerable populations like pregnant women (FASD) and adolescents (binge drinking). Furthermore, European Committee is regulating pricing, taxation and audiovisual commercial with the help of Council Directives. In Greece alcohol consumption is part of Mediterranean social life, so alcohol misuse is going underdiagnosed. Furthermore, it is well known that the amount of alcohol consumption has a direct relationship to the prevalence of problems experienced by that society and Greece has been in the middle of a huge financial crisis over the last decade. Greek Ministry of Health is planning to tackle harmful alcohol use by reorganizing services in the addiction field. Detox units, multiple intervention programs and mobile addiction units will be established and linked to the primary health care services. Alcohol misuse is a Public Health issue but also a key impact factor on a country's sustainable development.
