AB  - The author analyzes a study of 62 teens ordered by the Utah Second District Juvenile Court to complete the Drug School program. The program is aimed at decreasing drug abuse by improving communication within the family. Both teens and their parents participated in the program. The changes in attitudes between parents and teenagers were analyzed before and after their participation in the program. The program is comprised of both presentations and group discussions that focus on drug use and its effects, factors influencing drug use, and techniques for communicating effectively. The article includes statistical tables which show total offense rates, drug offense rates, and types of offenses and their frequency. Data is presented for each category for time periods both prior to and following program attendance.
