AB  - The article presents an author's insight regarding the relation between spirituality and clinical psychiatry. He states that the spiritual fellowship Alcoholics Anonymous (AA) aids to the practice of evidence-based addiction medicine. He also mentions that the Joint Commission on Accreditation of Healthcare Organizations requires spirituality in psychiatric assessment. An overview of the AA movement is offered. He suggests that there must be further research on the mechanisms underlying the effectiveness of the movement in order to understand how it promotes recovery for the patients.
