AB  - Presents a workplace mapping technique that identifies work group members who should be targeted as part of an accommodation intervention strategy & describes its use with 25 workers with a psychiatric disability in New York City; three cases are reviewed as examples. Results show that workplace mapping is an important companion to the intake interview. It helps focus on the workplace & clarifies a strategy for intervention by adding specificity about who offers the supports & which behaviors may serve as barriers. 2 Tables, 1 Figure, 36 References. Adapted from the source document.
