AB  - Investigated is whether the retention rate for a therapeutic community program for drug abusers could be increased using a short-term, cognitive-behavioral intervention. In a quasi-experimental, nonequivalent control group design involving 22 new admissions to such a program in Dade County, Fla, the Beck Depression Inventory & Problem-Solving Inventory were administered in pretest-posttest format, & the Client Satisfaction Questionnaire administered at posttreatment. After 60 days, results revealed a retention rate of 100% for the treatment group vs 27% for the untreated group. Results are discussed in terms of their applications to social work practice. 9 Tables, 28 References. Adapted from the source document.
