AB  - This article addresses costs and utilization for mental health/substance abuse treatment, with particular emphasis on the emerging importance of self-insured coverage in the 1990s. Drug abuse treatment demand and utilization are estimated with an insurance claims database from self-insured employers. The study population was selected from a large database consisting of health insurance claims for all treatment events starting Jan. 1, 1989 and ending December 31, 1991. Approximately three-quarters of the increase in inpatient usage attributable to fractional co-insurance is due to increased usage per person (the other 1/4 refers to increased numbers of users). About half of the increase in outpatient usage is due to increased usage per person. In summary, the estimates provide useful measurements of the potential impacts of improved drug abuse treatment coverage.
