AB  - In an exploration of how several standard psychosocial measures relate to drug treatment efficacy for prison releasees, 2 drug treatment programs for prison releasees (outpatient treatment & a therapeutic community setting) are compared with each other & to a comparison group of releasees. Treatment success is measured at 6 & 18 months after release from prison in terms of: (1) abstinence of drug &/or alcohol use, & (2) lack of recividism. Logistic regression analysis suggests that personality is related to treatment efficacy, sometimes in nonexpected ways. Results are discussed in terms of differences in client characteristics & treatment modalities.
