AB  - Authors are presenting challenges and specicities in group therapy of patients/prisoners that have Posttraumatic stress disorder or Personality disorder on Department of Forensic psychiatry in Prison hospital Zagreb and during the prison sentence are conducting the obligatory measurement of psychiatric treatment ordered by the Law (according to the article 68. of Croatian Criminal Act). Group has 10-12 members, it is half opened and it is hold ones a week for 60 minutes by psychiatrist on the CBT principles with the elements of support therapy and psycho education. The aims and effects of group treatment are presented and the challenges in therapeutic process are discussed, especially regarding the co morbidity of diagnosis as well as the possible conicts of interest and ethical dilemmas due to psychotherapeutic work in forensic psychiatry and penal conditions. [PUBLICATION ABSTRACT]
