AB  - Assessed the prevalence of irritable bowel syndrome in 47 patients with schizophrenia (mean age 37.4 yrs) compared to an age-matched control group of patients seeking treatment for other medical illnesses in a primary care clinic. Data were gathered via semi-structured interviews. Results showed that 19% of the disordered Ss met criteria for irritable bowel syndrome in contrast to the 2.5% of controls. Schizophrenic patients seldom complained of gastrointestinal symptoms until specifically asked. Therefore, it may be important to inquire about gastrointestinal problems before initiating pharmacotherapy in order to differentiate side effects from a preexisting condition. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved)
