AB  - This research examined how mental health and addiction services in the Northwest Area of British Columbia can improve service delivery, through existing clubhouse programs. Clubhouses are community mental health and addictions programs that provide psychosocial rehabilitation services to individuals with severe and persistent mental illness. The opportunity existed to determine what effective programming looks like in clubhouses. The project's findings may be useful in improving the functioning of mental health clubhouses, and in the process, increase the level of services provided to people with mental illness in the Northwest Area of British Columbia. The research involved focus groups and an online survey. The survey data was presented to focus group participants to develop recommendations for improving services in the area clubhouses. The resulting recommendations are aimed at having a positive influence on the recovery of mental health service recipients: a benefit that aligns with Northern Health's goals and strategies. Copies of dissertations may be obtained by addressing your request to ProQuest, 789 E. Eisenhower Parkway, P.O. Box 1346, Ann Arbor, MI 48106-1346. Telephone 1-800-521-3042; email: disspub@umi.com
