AB  - Studied the use of group psychotherapy in the care of 24 22–53 yr old schizophrenic outpatients. A matched control group was treated with neuroleptics. The group psychotherapy was conducted by the authors over 5 yrs, combined analytical, directive, and group dynamic strategies in its design, and took into consideration the vulnerabilities, ego weaknesses, and possible suicidal tendencies of the group. Results show a significant decrease in the number of clinical relapses for the Ss in group therapy, compared with the controls. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
