AB  - Like many agencies in the field of substance misuse, NORCAS works within the guidelines provided by Models of Care, as directed by the National Treatment Agency, through their local Drug Action Team. Around 15 per cent of clients are referred by other health professionals and 85 per cent self-refer. Severe and Enduring Mental Illness (SEMI) includes chronically ill people who have never received any form of counselling intervention. The way the healthcare system separates out issues may serve to fragment an individual even further. Many mental health trusts throughout the country highly value the service provided by the voluntary counselling sector. NORCAS is not funded to work specifically with dual diagnosis clients, yet these clients make up a high percentage of their client group.
