AB  - Objective: To investigate the the effects of positive psychological group counseling on the mental health of college students from low income family (CSLF). Methods: The experiment of using 2 × 2 multi-group (experimental group„ no -treatment control group) and multi-time sequence (pre-and post treatment, subsequent follow-ups) design was performed to study 80 CSLF in Qinghai and Ningxia provinces for half a year. Results: After group counseling, the scores of experimental group in GHQ-20 and index of well-being were significantly changed, while those of the control group had no significant difference. The results of follow-up showed that the effect of group counseling still existed after six months. Conclusion: Group counseling based on positive psychology can enhance the level of mental health, self-esteem and subjective happiness of CSLF, and decrease the level of their depression and anxiety. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
