AB  - The Theatre of the Now was a community-based project undertaken in Toronto, Canada to offer a series of dramatic presentations focused on mental health issues. Drama was used as a medium that would be engaging, entertaining, and nonthreatening, and that might serve to generate group discussions with members of audiences. It was hoped that audience participation in these discussions might enhance awareness of personal problems and stimulate interest in the effective utilization of community mental health facilities. The present authors discuss preparation prior to performances and performance format. Some of the variations are considered that were encountered in performances before different audiences, including students, adolescents affiliated with helping agencies, residents of rehabilitation homes or institutions, residents of housing units for the economically disadvantaged, members of private and closed psychotherapy groups, members of the general public, and staff of social service agencies. Reactions to the performance, effectiveness of the approach, and therapeutic effects of the program are also considered. (7 ref) (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
