AB  - The purpose of this dissertation is to present a program design for a comprehensiveday treatment program for older adults with late-onset substance abuse problems. For the purpose of this program an older adult will be defined as being over 55. Late-onset is defined as substance abuse starting after the age of 45. Research has indicated favorable outcomes for the elderly substance abusers in age-heterogeneous treatment programs (Atkinson, Tolson, & Turner, 1993) these studies have for the most part been limited to groups at Veterans Administration Hospitals; a largely male population. The older adults as a larger group have been found to have different needs from their younger counter parts (Johnson, 1989). Treatment programs specifically targeting older adult substance abusers are scarce (Johnson, 1989). The emphasis of the program will be on age-specific, group treatment approaches that provide support and avoid confrontation; attention to negative emotional states such as depression, loneliness, or overcoming losses; teaching skills to rebuild social supports; employing staff who are experienced in working with older persons, and have interest in doing so; comprehensive casemanagement; and modifying treatment to be appropriate for older adults. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
