AB  - Opioid addiction is a chronic disease necessitating community-based recovery management approaches for increased chances of patient recovery. Medication-assisted treatment (MAT) is the use of medications in combination with counseling and behavioral therapies to provide a whole patient approach to the treatment of substance use disorders. This dialogue is a critical one for the profession because social workers represent a significant share of the substance abuse treatment field and are often the ones that might have the power regarding treating or referring clients for the use of MATs, and in establishing policies for such treatment. To illuminate the ins and outs of MAT, the author met with an experienced group of Maintenance and Recovery Services (MARS) clinicians first in a focus group and then at the clinic setting, where the author was given a tour and an opportunity to meet with their patients as well. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2013 APA, all rights reserved). Adapted from the source document.
