AB  - The illegal use of drugs has grown at an alarming rate over recent decades, crossing all social, political, & national boundaries. Ordinarily, only one aspect of illicit drugs is considered problematic -- the addiction side of drugs. Unless there are a substantial number of addicts, people are not willing to consider use of illicit drugs as a problem. Primarily people look at one end of the drug problem continuum -- the consumption side. Bangladesh has an estimated 100,000 brown sugar abusers. The route or methods of drug use are also changing over time. There are injectors in Bangladesh. Drug addiction is becoming a national issue. Gradually treatment services are being developed in response. These services are explored here, drawing on a focus group meetings with representatives of drug treatment centers of the capital city, Dhaka. Highlighted are the nature & dynamics of the processes a poor country like Bangladesh uses to treat its own addicts.
