AB  - The purpose of this study was to examine the effects of risk-factor based cognitive-behavioral group therapy (CBGT) on the depressive symptoms as well as the Cortisol and inflammatory cytokine levels of the community-dwelling elderly with minor depression. Ten elderly participants attended the CBGT group and 10 attended the control group. The CBGT group held eight weekly 2-hour sessions, with the intervention foci in three modifiable risk factors of depression among elderly community subjects, including bereavement, sleep disturbance, and functional impairment. All the psychological variables, as well as the serum Cortisol, interleukin-6, and tumor necrosis factor–α levels of the participants were assessed at baseline and after intervention. The CBGT group showed significant improvement in depressive symptoms, sleep quality, function impairment; and higher level of TNF–α after intervention. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
