AB  - Research Objectives: To summarize the prevalence of osteoarthritis (OA) and its associated risks and costs. To report an exercise/health education program that is a clinically effective for post-surgical rehabilitation. Design(s): Fit & Strong! (F&S) is an exercise/health education program for older adults with lower extremity (LE) OA. It has been tested for efficacy (Hughes et al., 2004; 2006) using a randomized controlled trial comparing the intervention to a light health education group with follow-up at 2, 6, and 12 months. F&S was tested for effectiveness (Hughes et al., 2010) in a randomized trial that assigned participants to different maintenance options after the 8-week program ended with 2, 6, 12, and 18 month follow-ups. Setting(s): All testing occurred within Chicago community senior centers and housing. Participant(s): Efficacy (n=215) and effectiveness (n=419) were tested in older adults (>= 60) with rheumatologist-diagnosed LE OA. Intervention(s): The F&S intervention is offered 3 days/week for 8 weeks. Each session consists of 60 minutes of flexibility, low-impact aerobics, and progressive strength training followed by 30 minutes of health education and group problem solving. Main Outcome Measure(s): Exercise self-efficacy; exercise adherence; LE pain, stiffness, and function (WOMAC); LE strength (Chair Stands); physical function (6-Minute Walk); anxiety and depression. Result(s): Statistically significant between group improvements were seen in; exercise self-efficacy and adherence at 2, 6 and 12 months; LE strength (2, 6, 18 months); physical function (2, 6, 12, 18 months); LE pain and function (2, 6, 12 months); anxiety and depression (2, 6, 12, 18 months). Conclusion(s): The F&S program is low-cost, scalable, disseminable, and improves several key clinical outcomes of importance to older adults with joint and mobility issues. F&S has significant potential as a pre/rehabilitative intervention for LE joint replacement patients. Author(s) Disclosures: None. Keywords: Osteoarthritis, Arthroplasty, Replacement, Resistance Training, Exercise, Frail ElderlyCopyright © 2020
