AB  - Evaluated the effects of case management, the proximity of case manager to treatment facility, and telephone use on use of medical and mental health services by residential substance abuse treatment clients. 229 residential clients (average age 33 yrs) meeting Iowa Case Management Project criteria were randomly assigned to 1 of 4 conditions for a 12-mo period. Three groups received case management according to the Iowa Case Management model and differed according to the location of the case manager and use of a telecommunication system; Group 4 received standard treatment services. Results show that case managers located at the treatment facility increased Ss' use of substance abuse treatment and medical services. Use of mental health services did not vary by group. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
