AB  - Department specialized for treatment of drug addicts exists for many years within the Psychiatric clinic at University Hospital »Sestre milosrdnice«. According to its organization and methods it is a model program that justifies importance of a residential treatment as a necessary intervention within a framework of treatment process and comprehensive treatment for specific category of addicts. Realization: the average length of stay in a residential treatment is 18 days. Yearly, it is around 200 referrals and hospitalizations. In order to decrease a risk of continuation of drug abuse, impulsive leaving and premature treatment termination, the program is of a closed type. Upon a hospital-based program as a single intensive and necessary intervention, other objectively possible solutions for further follow-up and treatment process are suggested to the patient and his family. Indications for the referral: patients with conditions of chemical dependency that could not have been stabilized through outpatient treatment without the use of opiate agonists in heroin addicts. Due to limited capacity of the Department our priorities are given to younger addicts, addicts with severe depression or other psychiatric comorbidity, pregnant addicted women, war veterans with or without PTSD. Treatment goals: realistic treatment interventions (empowerment of addicts and their families in order to prepare them for possible outcomes of the disease, psycho-diagnostic assessment especially among other psychiatric comorbidity, abstinence capacity testing with or without appropriate psycho-pharmacotherapy). Program evaluation: is conducted through evaluation forms based on the assessment of the extent of achieved treatment outcome administered both by expert as well as patients themselves. Treatment specifics: program is tailored to individual needs, balanced group and individual psychotherapy, psycho-education and pharmacotherapy, continuous program evaluation and modification incorporating recent addiction topics, permanent group and individual therapy as well as treatment program self-assessment conducted by an expert team. [ABSTRACT FROM AUTHOR] Copyright of Alcoholism: Journal on Alcoholism & Related Addictions is the property of Center for Study & Control of Alcoholism & Addictions and its content may not be copied or emailed to multiple sites or posted to a listserv without the copyright holder's express written permission. However, users may print, download, or email articles for individual use. This abstract may be abridged. No warranty is given about the accuracy of the copy. Users should refer to the original published version of the material for the full abstract. (Copyright applies to all Abstracts.)
