AB  - INTERVENTION: Intervention 1: Research by providing a written reference from the relevant authorities in Sabzevar University of Medical Sciences and Research Introduction The aim of this study is expressed at the beginning of the questionnaire. After obtaining informed consent from the patients and their families can be assured that their data is confidential. Data collection included the Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Index (PSQI) and demographic information. The initial study (pre‐intervention), questionnaires completed by patients attending the patient fails to respond to questions, with permission, questionnaires, interviews will be completed. People who have poor sleep quality were identified and randomly assigned to the intervention or control groups are. After determining the control and intervention groups, applying CCM begins. Patients were divided into 7 groups (in terms of sample size in groups of 6‐12 individuals) are divided. Continuous care model includes four stages, orientation ( knowing how to interact with patients , families , nurses, explaining the model ) , sensitization (patient and family involvement in the implementation of continuing care approach ) , consultation to diagnose the needs of patients on average for each group of 6 ‐ 4 sessions ( lasting 1 to 2 hours ) in the past three weeks and is held twice in a week . Continuous care in the second stage of consultation, monitoring and evaluation is performed. The total running time of 3 months, each model is a three‐week period. Immediately after completion of the questionnaire models two intervention groups and the data analysis is complete. If the patient fails to attend more than two sessions, group discussions and consultations, are excluded. But the principles of analysis and sampling, in the final analysis are calculated. The control group did not receive any intervention after the completion of an educational booklet Counseling and group discussions are provided. Intervention 2: The control Lifestyle Research by providing a written reference from the relevant authorities in Sabzevar University of Medical Sciences and Research Introduction The aim of this study is expressed at the beginning of the questionnaire. After obtaining informed consent from the patients and their families can be assured that their data is confidential. Data collection included the Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Index (PSQI) and demographic information. The initial study (pre‐intervention), questionnaires completed by patients attending the patient fails to respond to questions, with permission, questionnaires, interviews will be completed. People who have poor sleep quality were identified and randomly assigned to the intervention or control groups are. After determining the control and intervention groups, applying CCM begins. Patients were divided into 7 groups (in terms of sample size in groups of 6‐12 individuals) are divided. Continuous care model includes four stages, orientation ( knowing how to inter The control group did not receive any intervention after the completion of an educational booklet Counseling and group discussions are provided. CONDITION: diabetes. ; Non‐insulin‐dependent diabetes mellitus E10‐E14 Non‐insulin‐dependent diabetes mellitus PRIMARY OUTCOME: Quality of sleep. Timepoint: Before and after. Method of measurement: Standardized questionnaire Pitts Burg. SECONDARY OUTCOME: Depression. Timepoint: before and after. Method of measurement: Standard questionnaire beck. INCLUSION CRITERIA: INCLUSION CRITERIA: Subjects, diabetic patients attending the Diabetes Clinic Sabzevar Inclusion criteria included: willingness to participate in research; Type 2 diabetes; Having diabetes clinic case study sites; Lack of mental retardation; lack of sleep disorders before the onset of diabetes; Lack of sleep medications during the study and the use and reporting are excluded. Having full awareness; listening and speaking ability acceptable to answer questions and they ranged in age from 40 to 65 years. Meanwhile, people either men or women; illiterate or literate; able to work, they can take part in this research. Exclusion criteria: Patients, who are not eligible for the above, plus a history of psychiatric disorders (Schizoid, anxiety, depression, and dementia) or psychiatric hospitalization for the above reasons, if any, are excluded.
