AB  - INTERVENTION: In this study, in control group, Alprazolam 0/5 mg/oral before sleeping for four consecutive weeks was used. In this study, Stroke foot massage was conducted in experimental group. Intervention was 5 minutes Stroke foot massage, three times a week for four excutive days in the evening and night shifts (because of closeness to the night sleeping hours) among male patients by researcher and female patients by trained female partner after declaration of patient readiness. Stroke foot massage perfomed in the sole of the foot with a mild to moderate pressure slowly and regularly in every direction. Intervention 1: In this study, Stroke foot massage was conducted in experimental group. Intervention was 5 minutes Stroke foot massage, three times a week for four excutive days in the evening and night shifts (because of closeness to the night sleeping hours) among male patients by researcher and female patients by trained female partner after declaration of patient readiness. Stroke foot massage perfomed in the sole of the foot with a mild to moderate pressure slowly and regularly in every direction. Intervention 2: In this study, in control group, Alprazolam 0/5 mg/oral before sleeping for four consecutive weeks was used. Treatment ‐ Drugs Treatment ‐ Other CONDITION: Nonorganic insomnia Sleep Quality. ; Nonorganic insomnia PRIMARY OUTCOME: Lack of sleep. Timepoint: Before intervention, a week later, two weeks later, three weeks later and four weeks later after beginning of intervention. Method of measurement: By using Pittsburg and Sleep Log. SECONDARY OUTCOME: Improving sleep Quality. Timepoint: Weekly. Method of measurement: By using Pittsburg and Sleep Log. INCLUSION CRITERIA: INCLUSION CRITERIA: Willingness to cooaperate and participate in research; giving informed consent; having sleep problems based on scores resulting from Pittsburg questionnaire; performing hemodialysis in the evening and night shifts; lack of amputation, injury, infection, wound and skin disease in the lower limbs; insensitive to massage and having endurance against massage by patient; not having clotting disorders, vascular, neuropathy and diabetes complications; age above 18 years and below 65 years; no history of psychiatric disorders or psychiatric hospitalization; not using hypnotic drugs. Exclusion criteria: Not wanting to continue working; referring to another facility for futher treatment; referring patients for kidney transplantation; having undiagnosed illnesses.
