rol group: Routine training will be conducted in the control group. After intervention, educational booklet will be given to the control group. Workshops: This program consist of 4 sessions of workshops (4 hour) during 4 weeks To facilitate the work, as well as increase performance classes, their intervention groups will be divided into smaller groups. So that workshop will be divided into 2 groups. The topics of the program include learning more about end stage renal disease, principle of self care, personal health, role planning and delegating tasks, promote of care skills, ways of increase confidence, reduce stress, time management, education to increase communication skills with friends and acquaintances. CONDITION: Extracorporeal dialysis hemodialysis. ; Extracorporeal dialysis PRIMARY OUTCOME: Burnout severity. Timepoint: before intervention and 1 week after intervention. Method of measurement: Zarit caregiver burden scale. INCLUSION CRITERIA: Include criteria: Age between 18‐60 years; Can read and right; Lack of mental illness and chronic physical and cognitive disorders, hearing and vision; Lack of use drugs and psychotropic substances; The care of patients have at least 6 months; Is not a member of the medical team; With the patient in one place to live; Are main caregivers; Orientation to Persian language; Access to cell phone or telephone; Be able to participate in training sessions; Don’t Participate in other educational classes. Exclude criteria: Don’t attend two training sessions; Death of the patient in during of this study; Don’t want to attend classes.
