AB  - INTERVENTION: Behavior In massage group, participants after pre‐test have the head and neck, back, arms and legs massage for 20 minutes, once a week during six weeks (from 22 to 28 weeks gestation) in training classes for mothers in health centers equipped with facilities such as appropriate mats. First session will take about half an hour and other sessions take 20 minutes. In the first session, it will be explained about the causes of anxiety and ways to control it and the purpose of the intervention. To maintain patient privacy, the room where massage will be done is equipped with thick curtains and paravan. To maintain more privacy for patients during the massage, the room doors will be locked to prevent possible entry and exit. In the guided imagery group, intervention after pre‐test will be done when participants receive the guided imagery techniques for 20 minutes, once a week during for six weeks (from 22 to 28 weeks gestation) in the training classes of health center. In addition, the registration daily workouts form will be given to the mothers. They have to listen to the CD in a quiet environment for 20 minutes every day, and insert it in the form. We called the mother twice a week while remind them of importance of exercise. Forms will be collected by a researcher at the next meeting. Intervention 1: In massage group, participants after pre‐test have the head and neck, back, arms and legs massage for 20 minutes, once a week during six weeks (from 22 to 28 weeks gestation) in training classes for mothers in health centers equipped with facilities such as appropriate mats. First session will take about half an hour and other sessions take 20 minutes. In the first session, it will be explained about the causes of anxiety and ways to control it and the purpose of the intervention. To maintain patient privacy, the room where massage will be done is equipped with thick curtains and paravan. To maintain more privacy for patients during the massage, the room doors will be locked to prevent possible entry and exit. Intervention 2: In the guided imagery group, intervention after pre‐test will be done when participants receive the guided imagery techniques for 20 minutes, once a week during for six weeks (from 22 to 28 weeks gestation) in the training classes of health center. In addition, the registration daily workouts form will be given to the mothers. They have to listen to the CD in a quiet environment for 20 minutes every day, and insert it in the form. We called the mother twice a week while remind them of importance of exercise. Forms will be collected by a researcher at the next meeting. Intervention 3: The control group will receive the routine and common care during pregnancy. At the end of the sixth week, we will call and invite them to participate in the post‐test. The control group will receive the routine and common care during pregnancy. At the end of the sixth week, we will call and invite them to participate in the post‐test. CONDITION: anxiety. ; Generalized anxiety disorder Generalized anxiety disorder PRIMARY OUTCOME: Anxiety. Timepoint: pre‐ intervention and 6 weeks after intervention. Method of measurement: Pregnancy related anxiety questionnaire ‐ revised. INCLUSION CRITERIA: INCLUSION CRITERIA: age between 18 and 35 years; singleton pregnancy; being in the second trimester (22 to 28 weeks of pregnancy); Iranian race; having literacy; lack of stressful life event during six months; disuse of any anti‐anxiety medication; do not use massage therapy and similar methods during pregnancy; lack of physical illness that has health risks for her and her fetus by massage such as spinal cord injury or surgery; the ability of the regular participation in meetings; no history of recurrent pregnancy loss; lack of drug addiction; lack of physical and mental illness; lack of obstetric complications such as cervical cerclage, placenta previa, high fever, premature rupture of membranesm, polyhydramnios. Exclusion criteria: the occurrence of stressful events or the creation of any obstetrical complication in the long run which has risk for the health of the mother or her baby such as high‐blood pressure during pregnancy; A skin lesion at the site of massa
