AB  - INTERVENTION: Intervention 1: This study has two groups. "Intervention group" 2. "Control group". The "intervention group" will receive a family‐based treatment plan based on the concepts of Johnson's drug adherence model. (Model of Conduct) A meeting will take place at the center and for the third concept (feedback) 2 home visits. Intervention 2: Control group: The "control group" receives routine care at the health center and at the end of the study the subject leaflet is distributed to the participants. CONDITION: hypertension. ; Essential (primary) hypertension PRIMARY OUTCOME: In this study, the effect of independent variable of family‐based diet regimen on blood pressure dependent variables (systolic and diastolic) in elderly patients with hypertension will be investigated. Timepoint: This study was performed before, immediately and three months after the intervention. Method of measurement: In this study, data collection tools are German Richter model mercury barometer, German Richter model medical device, Elderly Blood Pressure Checklist, Needs Assessment Questionnaire and Demographic Questionnaire and Disease Information. INCLUSION CRITERIA: 1. Elderly people who are diagnosed with hypertension and are treated by a specialist at the center. 2. Elderly people with hypertension referring to selected comprehensive health centers in Isfahan. 3. Be older than 60 years. 4.Elderly and family willing to participate in the study 5.Elderly not have known mental illness. 6. Familiar with Farsi language. 7.In the same intervention programs adherence to treatment regimen Do not have.
