dema Second session: general In the interference group based on the social network which consists of 35 people, after filling out the written consent form, the questionnaires of the fear of cancer recurrence, the effect of lymphedema on life, and Iranian version of the European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC) Quality of life questionnaire (QLQ‐C30) and it’s supplementary Breast Cancer‐Specific Quality of life questionnaire (QLQ_BR23) are filled out by people. To preserve the patients’ privacy and their numbers, on a Telegram™‐based channel the same educational content are taught five times on different days in the afternoon hours. Channel members can pose their questions and answers with the administrator of the channel (i.e. the researcher). Also, after posing the content, to make sure of receiving messages from all the members, they are each required to inform the administrator of the channel or give their opinion(s) after receiving the content. Members are reminded to use Telegram™ sof Intervention 1: In the in‐person interference group which consists of 35 people, after filling out the written consent form, the questionnaires of the fear of cancer recurrence, the effect of lymphedema on life, and the Iranian version of the European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC) Quality of life questionnaire (QLQ‐C30) and it’s supplementary Breast Cancer‐Specific Quality of life questionnaire (QLQ_BR23) are filled out by people. In seven groups of five, patients receive self‐management trainings in five sessions in the form of speech, group discussion and question and answer which last as long as 60 minutes, and based on the patients’ need for question and answer, as long as 90 minutes. At the end of the interference sessions, the CDs containing the educational materials are given to be reviewed at home. The educational content is as follows: First session: preventing stress, fear and the anxiety caused by breast cancer with a focus on lymphedema Second session: general skills for self‐management Third session: problem‐solving skill with an explanation on lymphedema and its side effects, ways to control lymphedema and the phases of the self‐management of lymphedema (the second phase of the standard treatment of lymphedema) Fourth session: decision making and the use of resources with an explanation on which phase of self‐management ought to be utilized according to their own condition Fifth session: cooperation with the treatment team and the implementation of the learned skills at home Research units are required to fill out the questionnaires of the fear of cancer recurrence, the degree of the effect of lymphedema on life, and the questionnaires of the quality of life on patients with cancer and breast cancer immediately after the sessions are over and after three months. Intervention 2: In the interference group based on the social network which consists of 35 people, after filling out the written consent form, the CONDITION: C50‐C50 Condition 1: breast cancer. Condition 2: lymphedema. ; Malignant neoplasm of breast ; Postmastectomy lymphoedema syndrome Malignant neoplasm of breast Postmastectomy lymphoedema syndrome PRIMARY OUTCOME: Fear of recurrence cancer. Timepoint: before,Immediately, 3 months after intervention. Method of measurement: short form of fear of progression questionnaire. Quality of life. Timepoint: before,Immediately, 3 months after intervention. Method of measurement: questionnaires of QLQ‐BR23,QLQC30 and LLIS. INCLUSION CRITERIA: INCLUSION CRITERIA: ‐ A record of confirmed cancer from phase 0 to 3 ‐ Having lymphedema confirmed by the doctor in the last recent year ‐ Being between 18 and 55 years of age ‐ Completion of the remedies ‐ Reading and writing literacy ‐ Being skilled enough at using Telegram™ ‐ Having access to the Internet and a cellphone ‐ No use of psychiatric treatments and psychological counseling after catching cancer ‐ No background in taking part