AB  - INTERVENTION: Intervention 1: Intervention group: Intervention according to a protocol called cognitive‐behavioral self‐care cognitive‐behavioral therapy, a guide for women, written by Dr. Michel Herring Cognitive‐behavioral counseling counselor in collaboration with the British Columbia mental health program, mental health services in British Columbia. The intervention was presented as 7 sessions of one‐hour cognitive‐behavioral group therapy once a week. The sessions include: providing information on depression, providing information on treatment options in women with depression during pregnancy and postpartum, including drug therapy and psychological treatments such as cognitive‐behavioral therapy, explaining cognitive‐behavioral therapy and its role in depression, Explain self���care and its importance, a description of different areas of self‐care such as nutrition, exercise and the way to incorporate and nurture each of these areas in the person's life, how to determine the goal of developing each of the areas of self‐care and learning to solve existing problems To make positive changes in life, educate all kinds of wrong thoughts Intensify depression, learn how to identify and challenge these ideas, and provide solutions to prevent the return of symptoms of depression. Intervention 2: Control group: The routine midwifery care group will receive a midwife from the health center and will be monitored for interventional factors. CONDITION: depression. ; Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified PRIMARY OUTCOME: Pregnancy Depression Score in Edinburgh Postpartum Depression Questionnaire. Timepoint: At the beginning of the study, immediately, 4 weeks and 8 weeks after the end of the intervention. Method of measurement: Edinburgh Postpartum Depression Questionnaire. INCLUSION CRITERIA: Gravid First Age of 15 to 45 years Ability to speak Persian Literacy reading and writing Earn score 10 to 15 from the Edinburgh Postpartum Depression Inventory Gestational age 22 to 26 weeks
