AB  - INTERVENTION: Intervention 1: Intervention group: The training program for the intervention group in the form of 5 sessions in groups of 10 people with emphasis on meaning therapy for one hour and once a week with one hour of homework is performed at the end of each session. Lectures, face‐to‐face training, and group discussion will be used. Mineralogy worked on the intervention group to gain the ability to reach the real self and broaden vision of oneself and the world around and clarify things that are present and future life. One gives meaning. This method emphasizes 4 important interests that are rooted in human existence: death, freedom, loneliness and meaninglessness. In the first session, introduction and explanation of menopausal physiology, in the second session, determination of treatment goals and discussion of members about the complications they experience and explanation of the existential roots of problems (existential crisis and lack of meaning). Selection and mental health in menopause Session 4: Discovering meaning through personal desires and strengthening members in lovemaking and accepting a sense of responsibility Session 5: Summarizing and evaluating sessions to achieve the desired goals. Intervention 2: Control group: The control group does not receive counseling, they only receive routine care at the health center. CONDITION: Condition 1: Early complications of menopause. Condition 2: General health. PRIMARY OUTCOME: Improving the early effects of menopause. Timepoint: before the intervention and immediately after the intervention and two months after the intervention. Method of measurement: Menopausal Complications Questionnaire or (MRS). SECONDARY OUTCOME: General health. Timepoint: Before the intervention and immediately after the intervention and two months after the intervention. Method of measurement: General Health Questionnaire. INCLUSION CRITERIA: Stop Menstruation for at least 12 Months Menopausal Women Aged 45‐60 Years Lack of Physical and Mental Illness Lack of Use Traditional Medicine and Herbal Medicines Lack of Use of Relaxation Do not Participate In Yoga Having at Least 5 Classes of Literacy (Reading and Writing)
