AB  - Examined sociodemographic variables and outcome of 46 institutionalized elderly persons who did/did not cope well with a therapeutic treatment policy and everyday work during 1983–1987. Properties of well-coping (WC) Ss (good adaptation to aging, nonproblematic behavior, and high satisfaction with life) were compared with those of Ss who did not cope well. WC Ss were discriminated by therapeutic community activity, current mental health, and a socioeconomically deprived childhood. Success of the therapeutic community method seems to require (1) active participation; (2) rest and reminiscence; and (3) support, holding, and psychiatric intervention. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
