AB  - Veterans diagnosed with PTSD have been found to engage in health risk behaviors that ultimately lead to premature mortality. These findings highlight the need to promote healthy behavioral practices in veterans diagnosed with PTSD. When considering methods for promoting the change of health risk behaviors, recent research suggests that motivational interviewing is an effective method for facilitating an intrinsic desire to make such changes across a wide range of behavioral domains. Therefore, the current project focused on developing a motivational interviewing group treatment protocol targeted toward reducing health risk behaviors in veterans diagnosed with PTSD. Furthermore, the Member Workbook is intended to serve as a component of the group treatment protocol and will provide a systematic vehicle for introducing health-related information and practical applications for group participation. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2020 APA, all rights reserved)
