AB  - An overview of the social history & characteristics of group homes serving people with severe & persistent mental disabilities. A review of the literature reveals that such group homes now actually serve, on either a temporary or long-term basis, only a small proportion of this population. Homes are defined with respect to issues of size, community location, & rehabilitative intent. The use of alternatives to the supervised group home, eg, adult residential care & supported housing, is described, evaluating positive & negative features of each type, as well as the effects on people living in them. Social issues surrounding the group home as a residential alternative are also discussed. 1 Table, 44 References. Adapted from the source document.
