AB  - Differences between white & ethnic clients' (total N = 132) psychosocial functioning, psychiatric & substance abuse symptomatology, & service utilization costs, drawn from longitudinal clinical trial data on the relative cost effectiveness of three specialized interventions for dual disorders, are examined, & results compared with the existing literature. Although ethnic clients received fewer supportive treatment services during the first 6 months of the intervention program, their overall outcomes were equivalent to those of white clients at 6 months. There were nonfunctioning or symptom outcome differences across the three treatment groups, but, in comparison to the behavioral-skills-training & case-management groups, the 12-step group had the highest intensive & supportive service costs over time & the greatest reductions in intensive service costs after 6 months. Clinical issues are described, & implications for more effectively serving dually diagnosed ethnic clients outlined. 3 Tables, 42 References. Adapted from the source document.
