AB  - Detoxified alcoholics in psychiatric hospitals of a West German large city are investigated with regard to the question who of them get recommendations for further rehabilitation: to take part in a self help group or therapy. Patient documentations of two years are analysed. Results show that few detoxified alcoholics get advice for further rehabilitation. These persons are socially more integrated than those without advice.
